Z||000000||Gokart||04-12-2000||10:14 PM||||Bought a soldering kit today to reattach my egr solenoid plug wires. What kind of solder should I use? I have 2 kinds. One lead free and one with %50 lead. Does it matter? TIA for replies.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||lawrence||04-12-2000||10:39 PM||||For this it probably won't matter.  I assume you bought rosin core solder.  If not, you will need to get some rosin flux.  Don't use acid flux or the wires will corrode.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||04-13-2000||05:10 PM||||FWIW... "Electronics" type solder is usually 60/40 (or thereabouts) tin/lead.  ||||reg||1
